Copy mode: a frame shown unfinished is copied again once its GPU work completes.

The gate in front of the panel copy waits for the GPU fence of a swap for at most 100 ms and then
copies the frame as it is (gpu_hold_timeouts). When that frame was the last before a static screen,
the half-drawn picture stayed: Liquid Glass (dock, search pill, Control Center platters) vanished
after a home-page swipe or a tap and came back only with the next full redraw (owner video
2026-11-23; 22 gate timeouts in that boot). Such a frame now keeps its surfaces held and is queued
again when its fence passes, unless a newer swap arrives first. sweetfb_recopy=0 turns it off; the
FB stats gain recopies=N.

